# WARP-8's generators (a kit's Steps list, "generate"; ui.c act_euclid, act_mutate, act_grids): each writes the
# pattern as one undo. EUCLID and MUTATE the lane shown, GRIDS the kit's first three keys
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
tap SEQ
expect page Steps
tapkey b0
# EUCLID: four hits over sixteen steps, on the beats
tap SEL
row EUCLID HITS
tap SEL
wait 40
said EUCLID
expect note 1 1 1 1
expect note 1 1 5 1
expect note 1 1 9 1
expect note 1 1 13 1
expect note 1 1 2 0
# five hits, turned two steps later: 3, 7, 10, 13, 16
tap SEL
row EUCLID HITS
turn ALGO 1
row EUCLID ROTATE
turn ALGO 2
tap SEL
wait 40
expect note 1 1 1 0
expect note 1 1 3 1
expect note 1 1 7 1
expect note 1 1 10 1
expect note 1 1 13 1
expect note 1 1 16 1
# undo: the four on the beats again
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
wait 40
expect note 1 1 1 1
expect note 1 1 3 0
# MUTATE at 100 %: the hits on the beats stay
tap SEL
row MUTATE
turn ALGO 7
tap SEL
wait 40
said MUTATED
expect note 1 1 1 1
expect note 1 1 5 1
expect note 1 1 9 1
expect note 1 1 13 1
# GRIDS at the map's middle, half full: a kick on the one; the snare's lane written (key 2 on step 5 or 13)
tap SEL
row GRIDS X
tap SEL
wait 40
said GRIDS
expect note 1 1 1 1
shot generators.png
